1
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:16,799
Lacheng Classic.

2
00:01:16,959 --> 00:01:17,640
Original Wort: eight.

3
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,680
Alcohol: 2.5%.

4
00:01:18,799 --> 00:01:19,560
The color is a bit dark.

5
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,319
Take a sniff.

6
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,959
Beer tasting really comes down to this:

7
00:01:25,319 --> 00:01:27,239
Use your eyes to check the clarity,

8
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:29,159
look at the bubbles and the foam,

9
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:30,519
use your nose to smell the aroma,

10
00:01:30,959 --> 00:01:32,439
and then taste it with your mouth.

11
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,599
Then see if, after swallowing,

12
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:36,040
the aroma still lingers in your nose.

13
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,560
Mass-market beer doesn't need fancy flavors,

14
00:01:39,799 --> 00:01:40,959
but it must have good mouthfeel

15
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:42,200
and a touch of savoriness.

16
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,439
So which kind do you like best?

17
00:01:45,879 --> 00:01:46,840
I don't really like drinking,

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:47,840
and I can't drink, either.

19
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:49,200
Because of my job,

20
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,719
we can't eat spicy

21
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:51,840
or heavily seasoned food.

22
00:01:52,319 --> 00:01:54,480
Otherwise, it dulls our taste sensitivity.

23
00:01:54,799 --> 00:01:56,400
So for this job,

24
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,239
you have to sacrifice a lot.

25
00:01:58,799 --> 00:01:59,920
Isn't that just part of it?

26
00:02:03,239 --> 00:02:04,000
Xuemei,

27
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,840
why did you join the brewery buyout plan?

28
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,840
When we all pull together,

29
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,560
there's hope for the future.

30
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,280
Lapi Brewery is our home,

31
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,639
and we all love it.

32
00:02:14,319 --> 00:02:15,080
Well said!

33
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,240
Anyway,

34
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,080
our fate,

35
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:03,240
shouldn't it be in our own hands?

36
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:04,639
Right?

37
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,759
Just look around.

38
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:09,120
Who doesn't know people who got laid off?

39
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,039
What kind of life are they living?

40
00:04:14,039 --> 00:04:16,480
Want to sell tea eggs on the street,

41
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,199
scrub backs at a bathhouse,

42
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,040
or would you rather

43
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,000
stay right here

44
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:23,560
and build something great together?

45
00:04:25,839 --> 00:04:26,720
This critical question

46
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,319
is staring every one of us in the face.

47
00:04:28,319 --> 00:04:29,959
It couldn't be more urgent.

48
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,879
I've only got one idea:

49
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,680
we pool our money,

50
00:04:40,279 --> 00:04:41,879
and buy the factory ourselves.

51
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:46,560
Bottom line:

52
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,720
not for anyone else,

53
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:50,879
but for ourselves!

54
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:57,839
Who's in this with me?

55
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:16,879
I'm in!

56
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,920
Unity is strength!

57
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,720
We must take our destiny

58
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:23,600
into our own hands!

59
00:05:58,639 --> 00:05:59,000
Cheers!

60
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,240
If my mentor does it,

61
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:10,839
I'll do it too.

62
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,279
Let's do it!

63
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:28,759
Drink up!

64
00:06:34,639 --> 00:06:35,120
Bottoms up!

65
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:36,560
Count me in.

66
00:06:39,439 --> 00:06:39,839
Down it!

67
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:43,560
I'll drink for you!

68
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,120
I'll drink too!

69
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,439
Drink for me too!

70
00:06:48,519 --> 00:06:49,240
I'll drink for you!

71
00:06:51,959 --> 00:06:53,720
Come on, finish it off!

72
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,399
Give it to me! Give it!

73
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:57,759
Leave some for Workshop Two!

74
00:06:58,399 --> 00:06:59,439
Look at you, craving it all day.

75
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,199
Here!

76
00:07:00,199 --> 00:07:00,959
Holy crap!

77
00:07:01,079 --> 00:07:01,720
He drank the whole thing!

78
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,319
Gave me a fright!

79
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:03,399
Gather in closer!

80
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:04,600
Come on, get over here!

81
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,199
Listen up, folks.

82
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:07,680
Let me make this clear first.

83
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:09,399
I, Cheng Youtian,

84
00:07:09,639 --> 00:07:10,439
am a bachelor with nothing to lose.

85
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:11,879
I'm not afraid of retaliation.

86
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,360
Whoever wants to join together

87
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:18,360
to buy out and protect our factory,

88
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,639
you can sign up now.

89
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,160
Come on, sign up with Tu Chunyan!

90
00:07:33,959 --> 00:07:37,079
The old Lacheng Brewery,

91
00:07:37,759 --> 00:07:41,160
Filled with hope and sunshine.

92
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:44,800
The fragrance of our beer

93
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:48,680
Spreads far and wide.

94
00:08:42,279 --> 00:08:42,759
Leshui!

95
00:08:44,919 --> 00:08:45,440
Leshui!

96
00:08:45,759 --> 00:08:46,480
It's Haipeng!

97
00:08:47,279 --> 00:08:47,840
Leshui!

98
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:49,759
It's me, Haipeng!

99
00:08:57,879 --> 00:08:58,879
Wh-What's going on?

100
00:09:02,679 --> 00:09:03,480
Cao Jun is dead.

101
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,399
A black plastic bag over his head,

102
00:09:07,399 --> 00:09:08,840
clutching a beer bottle cap in his hand.

103
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:11,159
Exactly the same way Ma Guowen died.

104
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,320
When?

105
00:09:12,399 --> 00:09:13,279
No idea.

106
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,240
Tieping found him early this morning.

107
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,120
Anyway, everyone out there is in a panic.

108
00:09:19,639 --> 00:09:22,399
No one knows who's next.

109
00:09:23,519 --> 00:09:25,039
I just saw him earlier today.

110
00:09:25,559 --> 00:09:26,120
You saw him?

111
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:27,159
In the courtyard.

112
00:09:27,639 --> 00:09:28,080
Listen to me.

113
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,600
Don't you dare go around saying that.

114
00:09:30,799 --> 00:09:31,600
The neighbor across the hall

115
00:09:31,639 --> 00:09:33,240
was already hauled in by the cops for questioning.

116
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:34,879
So don't you get dragged into this.

117
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:35,559
Got it?

118
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,159
That's not up to me.

119
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:48,320
Leshui,

120
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,320
you should really leave Lacheng.

121
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,639
But the house hasn't sold yet.

122
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:57,600
Come on, look what's happening now.

123
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,360
Who has the mind to buy a house now?

124
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:00,279
Exactly.

125
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,480
The buyers looking at the place lately

126
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,759
are using the murders to lower the price.

127
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,279
So if the price isn't right,

128
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,679
don't rush to sell it off.

129
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,440
If you need money urgently,

130
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:07,919
you can ask me.

131
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:08,519
No, no, no need.

132
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,000
What you lent me before,

133
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,879
I haven't even paid back yet.

134
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,000
Once things get better,

135
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,720
I'll pay you back.

136
00:10:13,039 --> 00:10:14,320
Can we drop this for now?

137
00:10:14,639 --> 00:10:16,200
Safety is what matters most right now.

138
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,720
Don't you think

139
00:10:19,559 --> 00:10:21,799
one person killed Ma Guowen and Cao Jun?

140
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,960
Both had black plastic bags,

141
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:24,879
and both had a bottle cap.

142
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:27,960
Not necessarily.

143
00:10:29,679 --> 00:10:31,480
I saw how Ma Guowen ended up.

144
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,639
Kneeling on the train tracks,

145
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:34,600
hunched over,

146
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:35,919
put on public display.

147
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,320
It was a way of atoning for sin.

148
00:10:37,759 --> 00:10:38,919
It means the killer

149
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,639
held a massive grudge against him.

150
00:10:40,879 --> 00:10:42,559
But who could have a grudge against Cao Jun?

151
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:46,879
Exactly.

152
00:10:49,799 --> 00:10:51,399
Who could hold a grudge against Cao Jun?

153
00:10:56,279 --> 00:10:58,000
I think that cop is suspicious.

154
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,519
A cop?

155
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:05,600
How did you get tangled up with a cop?

156
00:11:06,679 --> 00:11:07,120
Look,

157
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,039
Leshui, listen to me.

158
00:11:09,879 --> 00:11:10,559
Just listen to me.

159
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:11,720
Leave here right away.

160
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,399
Weren't you going to Yunnan to do business?

161
00:11:13,399 --> 00:11:14,240
Just go, right now.

162
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:15,960
If you're short on cash, come to me.

163
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:16,879
J-Just consider it a loan.

164
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,200
I used to think

165
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,799
I was done with Lapi Brewery.

166
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:21,080
But over the past few days,

167
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,840
I watched that discarded footage again.

168
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,600
I want to take all this scrap footage

169
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,000
and re-edit it into a new film.

170
00:11:29,159 --> 00:11:32,000
This scrap footage looks so precious now.

171
00:11:32,159 --> 00:11:34,000
I wouldn't have it without your help.

172
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,519
If you're willing,

173
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:37,360
we could make "The New Malt Kingdom."

174
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,399
Didn't you say back then

175
00:11:39,399 --> 00:11:41,200
that this was for our kids and grandkids?

176
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,279
Now you're about to be a father.

177
00:11:43,639 --> 00:11:44,919
Don't you want your kid to see

178
00:11:44,919 --> 00:11:46,200
how great their dad was back in the day?

179
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,639
What greatness?

180
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:54,120
It's been so many years.

181
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:56,120
Who cares about that anymore?

182
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:58,159
No one will watch no matter how you edit.

183
00:11:59,879 --> 00:12:01,679
Leshui, let's be realistic.

184
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:03,960
Take Cao Jun.

185
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:07,000
Such an honest man,

186
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:07,960
and even he was murdered.

187
00:12:09,519 --> 00:12:10,200
Let me tell you,

188
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,799
I really feel like

189
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,919
this killer

190
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,080
is very likely

191
00:12:16,279 --> 00:12:17,639
coming after the old-timers

192
00:12:17,639 --> 00:12:18,679
who sold off the factory back then.

193
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,000
So what happened in the past, you really

194
00:12:22,559 --> 00:12:23,240
can't bring it up anymore.

195
00:12:30,879 --> 00:12:31,279
And another thing,

196
00:12:32,279 --> 00:12:33,360
those old materials of yours,

197
00:12:34,279 --> 00:12:36,000
I don't think they're safe here.

198
00:12:37,399 --> 00:12:39,080
I happen to have a big safe at my place.

199
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:40,639
Let me take them over for you.

200
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:41,159
Alright?

201
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:41,919
No need, no need.

202
00:12:42,039 --> 00:12:42,960
It's fine, it's fine.

203
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:43,679
Just hurry up and go home.

204
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:44,720
No, let me take them. Look after Lili.

205
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:46,200
Just take good care of Lili, okay?

206
00:12:46,559 --> 00:12:47,440
You're really something.

207
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:49,240
Once you make up your mind,

208
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,360
nothing can change it.

209
00:12:50,679 --> 00:12:51,080
Right.

210
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,440
Haven't I always been like this?

211
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:53,360
Just hurry up and head back.

212
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:53,720
No, no, no.

213
00:12:53,759 --> 00:12:54,399
I'm not finished yet.

214
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:56,840
Let me warn you.

215
00:12:57,679 --> 00:12:58,639
Those old-timers from back then,

216
00:12:58,919 --> 00:12:59,559
stay away from them.

217
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,360
Man,

218
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,360
who the good guys are

219
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:01,840
and who the enemies are,

220
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,639
you really can't tell.

221
00:13:02,759 --> 00:13:04,200
Why are you nagging so much?

222
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:04,879
Got it, got it.

223
00:13:04,879 --> 00:13:05,720
Hurry up and head back.

224
00:13:06,159 --> 00:13:06,919
Go on, get moving.

225
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:07,799
I'm leaving then.

226
00:13:07,879 --> 00:13:08,480
Go ahead, go on.

227
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,039
You stay safe, okay?

228
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:13,480
By the way,

229
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,840
you've got to change this lock.

230
00:13:14,879 --> 00:13:15,720
Got it? - Yeah, yeah.

231
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:16,120
It's too old.

232
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:16,519
Alright, alright, alright.

233
00:13:16,559 --> 00:13:17,000
I know, I know.

234
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,600
Hurry home. - You need a new one.

235
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:38,759
Hey, Sis.

236
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,720
A buddy of mine just opened a pub.

237
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,480
How about dropping by?

238
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,039
Your buddy opened it,

239
00:13:43,039 --> 00:13:44,360
not you.

240
00:13:46,639 --> 00:13:48,279
Once you open your own place,

241
00:13:48,639 --> 00:13:49,600
I'll think about it.

242
00:13:50,919 --> 00:13:51,519
That's why they say

243
00:13:51,519 --> 00:13:53,320
nothing gets past your sharp eyes.

244
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,360
It's actually mine.

245
00:13:55,039 --> 00:13:55,639
So, what do you say, Sis?

246
00:13:55,639 --> 00:13:56,840
Come check it out

247
00:13:57,159 --> 00:13:57,879
and give us some feedback?

248
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,679
Send me the address, then.

249
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,320
All right!

250
00:14:01,559 --> 00:14:02,120
Thanks, Sis!

251
00:14:02,159 --> 00:14:02,960
We'll be waiting for you!

252
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,320
I'll send you the location now.

253
00:14:11,879 --> 00:14:12,600
Sis,

254
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,960
thanks so much for coming.

255
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,240
How do you like my place?

256
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,159
Not bad.

257
00:14:17,679 --> 00:14:19,480
I prepared some great steak just for you,

258
00:14:19,519 --> 00:14:20,480
plus red wine,

259
00:14:20,519 --> 00:14:21,720
beer, liquor, and whiskey.

260
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:22,519
Take your pick.

261
00:14:22,559 --> 00:14:23,879
No need. Let's get down to business.

262
00:14:24,759 --> 00:14:25,879
Actually, the reason I invited you over

263
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,240
was to talk business, too.

264
00:14:27,279 --> 00:14:27,960
Then right this way, please.

265
00:14:28,879 --> 00:14:29,279
Sis,

266
00:14:29,759 --> 00:14:30,679
remember how you asked me

267
00:14:30,679 --> 00:14:32,080
to look into Gao Xuelin?

268
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:32,960
I found something.

269
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:34,440
He's a detective.

270
00:14:34,559 --> 00:14:35,200
A detective.

271
00:14:35,679 --> 00:14:36,679
And he's right here in Lacheng.

272
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,600
Then he must be really busy right now.

273
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,960
With the serial murders at Lapi Brewery.

274
00:14:41,279 --> 00:14:43,120
Your previous film, Malt Kingdom,

275
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,159
was about Lapi Brewery too.

276
00:14:44,519 --> 00:14:46,720
The workers lost the buyout to Ma Guowen.

277
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:48,279
Over a decade later,

278
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,559
the moment you returned to Lacheng,

279
00:14:49,919 --> 00:14:51,559
Ma Guowen invited you to shoot a film.

280
00:14:52,159 --> 00:14:53,519
Yet the very next day when shooting began,

281
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:56,360
you filmed the scene of Ma Guowen's death.

282
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:59,120
With your sharp instincts,

283
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:01,559
you must've realized the past and present

284
00:15:01,559 --> 00:15:02,480
are bound to be connected.

285
00:15:02,879 --> 00:15:04,480
We could definitely make a major,

286
00:15:04,759 --> 00:15:06,519
hard-hitting investigative piece.

287
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,159
And didn't another person die recently?

288
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:12,720
A former forklift driver at Lapi Brewery.

289
00:15:13,759 --> 00:15:15,159
Judging by his age,

290
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:17,799
he was probably in that buyout too.

291
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,120
You sure know a lot,

292
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:21,919
Li Mingyang.

293
00:15:22,519 --> 00:15:23,840
Then let me tell you a secret.

294
00:15:25,879 --> 00:15:27,120
In the Ma Guowen case,

295
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,840
one of the detectives on the task force

296
00:15:34,519 --> 00:15:35,480
is Gao Xuelin.

297
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:40,879
Ever since he questioned me at the station,

298
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,600
I found him a bit strange.

299
00:15:43,559 --> 00:15:44,679
Later, when he came to my place,

300
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,919
he clearly saw my hidden camera,

301
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,559
yet pretended not to notice,

302
00:15:50,159 --> 00:15:50,879
and didn't report it.

303
00:15:51,639 --> 00:15:52,360
Then,

304
00:15:53,279 --> 00:15:55,080
he asked to see my unused footage.

305
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,120
After I turned him down,

306
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,120
he still didn't give up

307
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,879
and kept digging.

308
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,799
All these moves of his

309
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,000
point to a single target:

310
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:06,440
Liu Xuemei.

311
00:16:06,879 --> 00:16:08,840
The Beer Taster who froze to death in '99.

312
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:09,799
He wants to know

313
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,840
what happened the day Liu Xuemei died.

314
00:16:12,679 --> 00:16:16,039
A detective on the Ma Guowen case

315
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:18,120
focusing so much on someone unrelated,

316
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,720
who was ruled over a decade ago

317
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:24,840
to have died a natural death—Liu Xuemei.

318
00:16:25,559 --> 00:16:27,039
Isn't that strange?

319
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:28,720
Very strange.

320
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,679
What's even stranger

321
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,039
is that he seems to do all this

322
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:33,399
behind his superiors' backs.

323
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,399
I think

324
00:16:38,159 --> 00:16:40,000
he's using his position

325
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,080
to do something else.

326
00:16:42,679 --> 00:16:44,240
Is he trying to uncover something,

327
00:16:44,919 --> 00:16:46,320
or cover something up?

328
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,240
I think

329
00:16:48,519 --> 00:16:50,159
there's definitely something wrong with him.

330
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:54,879
Then let's first

331
00:16:54,879 --> 00:16:56,399
dig into his background,

332
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:58,279
and find out what his connection

333
00:16:58,279 --> 00:16:59,240
to Liu Xuemei really is.

334
00:17:00,279 --> 00:17:02,519
The police are busy solving cases now.

335
00:17:02,519 --> 00:17:03,320
Let's not get in their way.

336
00:17:04,559 --> 00:17:06,720
Whatever personal info you find on Gao,

337
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,920
don't leak it under any circumstances.

338
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,480
Don't act on your own.

339
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:13,680
Understood.

340
00:17:18,839 --> 00:17:20,920
This is the card from your camera.

341
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,359
We've already looked through it.

342
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,200
Nothing wrong with it.

343
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:23,960
You can take it back.

344
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,960
Though, when you have time,

345
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:29,680
can I see your old unused footage?

346
00:17:31,279 --> 00:17:31,799
Sure.

347
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:33,799
Come by whenever you're free.

348
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,599
Just not Gao Xuelin.

349
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,119
That kid is still young.

350
00:17:40,759 --> 00:17:41,759
He's a bit too blunt.

351
00:17:43,079 --> 00:17:43,880
Where's he from?

352
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:44,960
Qingzhou.

353
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,680
Doesn't he have any relatives

354
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,519
or family living in Lacheng?

355
00:17:49,839 --> 00:17:50,359
Why?

356
00:17:50,759 --> 00:17:52,119
Why the sudden interest in him?

357
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:53,400
Just curious.

358
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,240
Curiosity killed the cat, you know.

359
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,240
Aren't we old classmates?

360
00:17:58,279 --> 00:17:59,480
Can't old classmates tell the truth?

361
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:00,440
Old classmates, right.

362
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,119
Do you even know my name?

363
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:03,640
Sun Jinfu.

364
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:05,880
Right.

365
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,039
My name is Sun Jinfu.

366
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,799
Gao Xuelin isn't a local,

367
00:18:12,119 --> 00:18:13,799
and has no family here.

368
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:16,839
Yet he asked about Liu Xuemei right away.

369
00:18:17,519 --> 00:18:19,039
When that happened to Liu Xuemei,

370
00:18:19,119 --> 00:18:20,200
he must've been very young.

371
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:22,720
So why does he know so much

372
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,759
about the old Lapi Brewery?

373
00:18:29,599 --> 00:18:31,200
I've noted down everything you reported.

374
00:18:35,079 --> 00:18:36,559
We have a vetting department here.

375
00:18:36,799 --> 00:18:37,599
Don't worry.

376
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:40,599
You might not want to hear this,

377
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,319
but you should worry more about yourself.

378
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:45,960
Did you sell that house?

379
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:47,599
Found a buyer yet?

380
00:18:51,599 --> 00:18:52,319
As a detective,

381
00:18:52,319 --> 00:18:53,519
having done this for so many years,

382
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:54,279
let me tell you,

383
00:18:54,279 --> 00:18:56,039
all the weird people and bizarre things...

384
00:18:56,039 --> 00:18:56,640
there's plenty out there.

385
00:18:57,119 --> 00:18:58,039
And working as a journalist,

386
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,279
you must've seen quite a lot too.

387
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:02,319
But I think a detective's mindset

388
00:19:02,519 --> 00:19:04,039
and a journalist's mindset...

389
00:19:04,359 --> 00:19:05,000
are different.

390
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:06,920
Think about it.

391
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,839
For a cop,

392
00:19:09,079 --> 00:19:10,680
nothing surprises them.

393
00:19:11,279 --> 00:19:12,039
As for journalists,

394
00:19:12,599 --> 00:19:14,359
the weirder, the better.

395
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,519
They dread the ordinary.

396
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:18,640
Right?

397
00:19:20,039 --> 00:19:20,839
When you've seen too much,

398
00:19:21,759 --> 00:19:23,000
what's normal feels abnormal,

399
00:19:23,559 --> 00:19:25,000
and what's abnormal feels normal.

400
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:27,880
Thank you, Officer Han.

401
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:28,839
Goodbye.

402
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,599
Take care.

403
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,160
Why did she call you Sun Jinfu?

404
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:37,839
My stage name.

405
00:19:39,039 --> 00:19:39,839
Stage name?

406
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:01,400
Liu Tieping!

407
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:03,440
Cao Jun is dead.

408
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,079
Tieping found him.

409
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:11,759
Liu Tieping!

410
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:15,079
Liu Tieping!

411
00:20:15,119 --> 00:20:16,240
It's me, Shen Leshui!

412
00:20:16,519 --> 00:20:17,319
Remember me?

413
00:20:23,559 --> 00:20:24,359
Liu Tieping!

414
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,680
Liu Tieping!

415
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:28,720
Driver!

416
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,720
Catch up to that guy ahead!

417
00:20:31,119 --> 00:20:32,240
I'll pay you double!

418
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:33,480
Deal.

419
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,720
Pay upfront.

420
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:38,599
Liu Tieping!

421
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,319
Driver, here's the money!

422
00:20:46,759 --> 00:20:48,240
Liu Tieping, stop running!

423
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:50,880
Liu Tieping!

424
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,680
Liu Tieping, stop running!

425
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,440
Liu Tieping!

426
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:11,799
Oh, come on...

427
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,160
Liu Tieping!

428
00:21:17,279 --> 00:21:18,680
Why are you running?

429
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,720
You didn't do anything wrong!

430
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:21,400
Why run?

431
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,359
Because you're chasing me!

432
00:21:24,039 --> 00:21:24,480
If you didn't run,

433
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,480
why would I chase you?

434
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:26,200
No!

435
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,880
I ran because you were chasing me!

436
00:21:28,559 --> 00:21:29,960
Why would I chase you if you didn't run?

437
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,640
You found Cao Jun this morning, right?

438
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,319
Go ask the cops!

439
00:21:40,839 --> 00:21:41,640
Who do you think

440
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,279
killed Cao Jun?

441
00:21:44,759 --> 00:21:45,240
Hey,

442
00:21:45,359 --> 00:21:46,559
I'm not a cop!

443
00:21:48,279 --> 00:21:49,519
Cao Jun and Ma Guowen...

444
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,119
Who else were they tied up with?

445
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,559
Ask the cops!

446
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:54,720
One last question.

447
00:21:55,079 --> 00:21:55,920
Just one last question.

448
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,680
Liu Xuemei had a kid.

449
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,240
How old back then?

450
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:03,039
Why are you asking about that?

451
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,160
Since I can't leave Lacheng right now,

452
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,440
I've been going through discarded footage.

453
00:22:10,279 --> 00:22:11,440
I saw Sister Xuemei.

454
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:14,720
Seven or eight, I guess.

455
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,400
Do you know who she was close to

456
00:22:18,839 --> 00:22:20,079
back in those days?

457
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,279
Who were her closest friends?

458
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,160
I don't know.

459
00:22:43,319 --> 00:22:43,799
Need something?

460
00:22:45,799 --> 00:22:46,519
"Need something?"

461
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,359
You're asking me?

462
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:51,519
You're hilarious.

463
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:54,400
In a Lacheng putting on an act contest,

464
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,400
you'd definitely take first prize.

465
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,799
I don't get what you're trying to say.

466
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:03,880
Let's go to your room.

467
00:23:04,160 --> 00:23:04,680
Too chaotic out here.

468
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,480
What do you want, anyway?

469
00:23:10,839 --> 00:23:12,119
Come to the police station with me.

470
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:13,880
In front of me,

471
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:15,279
tell the police clearly

472
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,839
that I'm not a suspect.

473
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,279
Why would you be a suspect?

474
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,279
Didn't you report me?

475
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,440
Stop playing dumb.

476
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,319
I reported you?

477
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,400
Yeah.

478
00:23:28,759 --> 00:23:29,720
You told the police.

479
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:32,440
You said I was with Cao Jun last night.

480
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,680
Now Cao Jun is dead,

481
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:34,720
and they suspect me.

482
00:23:35,359 --> 00:23:35,920
What happened to you?

483
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,039
Wasn't it you who reported me?

484
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:38,559
They hauled me in and grilled me.

485
00:23:39,359 --> 00:23:40,279
Well, let me tell you,

486
00:23:40,599 --> 00:23:41,319
I didn't report you.

487
00:23:42,559 --> 00:23:44,000
Not a word out of your mouth is true.

488
00:23:46,839 --> 00:23:47,640
I know.

489
00:23:48,319 --> 00:23:49,480
None of you like me.

490
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:52,720
Just because "Malt Kingdom"

491
00:23:52,799 --> 00:23:54,039
didn't turn out the way you wanted,

492
00:23:56,119 --> 00:23:57,319
you think I'm a traitor

493
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:59,480
who sold out to Ma Guowen.

494
00:24:01,279 --> 00:24:02,359
Well, let me tell you,

495
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:04,359
I'm sick of it too.

496
00:24:07,039 --> 00:24:08,359
I thought it was easy money,

497
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:10,119
right when I needed cash most,

498
00:24:10,119 --> 00:24:11,480
a chance to make a quick buck came along.

499
00:24:11,599 --> 00:24:12,200
And what happened?

500
00:24:12,319 --> 00:24:13,559
Stuck here and can't go back to Beijing.

501
00:24:15,079 --> 00:24:16,279
You're short on cash too?

502
00:24:16,759 --> 00:24:18,519
Guess you're not doing well in Beijing.

503
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,720
Do you own a place in Beijing?

504
00:24:22,839 --> 00:24:23,559
Haven't bought a car either, right?

505
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:27,400
So you're just one of those legendary

506
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,480
Beijing drifters?

507
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:29,359
Yeah.

508
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:31,599
I was just a contract worker.

509
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:34,039
When they downsized,

510
00:24:34,359 --> 00:24:35,160
people like me were the ones cut.

511
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,240
You got laid off?

512
00:24:39,079 --> 00:24:39,599
Serves you right.

513
00:24:41,559 --> 00:24:43,839
I thought the world couldn't hold you.

514
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,880
Think about it carefully.

515
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:49,799
The two people who died

516
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,640
were both from the old Lapi Brewery.

517
00:24:52,799 --> 00:24:54,440
And Liu Xuemei from over a decade ago.

518
00:24:55,079 --> 00:24:56,079
We knew all of them.

519
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,000
So what?

520
00:24:58,799 --> 00:25:00,240
Wanna bury the three of them together?

521
00:25:02,559 --> 00:25:03,799
I want to know

522
00:25:04,279 --> 00:25:05,279
how these cases

523
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:06,599
are connected.

524
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:09,200
I want to know who the killer is.

525
00:25:09,599 --> 00:25:10,680
Will he stop?

526
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:12,000
Will anyone else die?

527
00:25:13,839 --> 00:25:15,319
Only by finding the killer soon

528
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:18,039
can we prevent more murders.

529
00:25:19,279 --> 00:25:20,920
You must be out of your mind.

530
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:23,559
Why get tangled up in murder cases?

531
00:25:24,079 --> 00:25:25,000
Let me tell you,

532
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,799
I'm staying out of this.

533
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,359
I was honest with you,

534
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:32,720
so be honest with me.

535
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,240
Did you see Cao Jun yesterday?

536
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:35,640
What did he say?

537
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,440
Who do you think you are, a cop?

538
00:25:38,079 --> 00:25:39,039
Interrogating me?

539
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:41,000
Why should I tell you anything?

540
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:43,039
I'll only say this to the police.

541
00:25:43,039 --> 00:25:44,039
What business is it of yours?

542
00:25:52,039 --> 00:25:52,599
Shen Leshui.

543
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:54,359
How about

544
00:25:54,799 --> 00:25:56,400
we just get out of this dump?

545
00:25:57,279 --> 00:25:58,440
It's terrifying.

546
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,880
People are dying every few days.

547
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,799
Neither of us can leave right now.

548
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,880
The one who killed Ma Guowen and Cao Jun...

549
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:07,960
is it the same person,

550
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:08,960
or someone else?

551
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:09,759
What's the motive?

552
00:26:09,759 --> 00:26:10,519
If we don't figure it out,

553
00:26:10,519 --> 00:26:12,000
none of us can live in peace.

554
00:26:32,519 --> 00:26:33,440
You just said

555
00:26:33,839 --> 00:26:34,720
that Ma Guowen

556
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:36,160
and Cao Jun

557
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,599
are both from the old Lapi Brewery.

558
00:26:41,559 --> 00:26:42,240
Do you think

559
00:26:43,039 --> 00:26:45,599
the two of them were involved

560
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,400
in Liu Xuemei's death back then?

561
00:26:50,519 --> 00:26:51,440
Over the years,

562
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:53,640
you've stayed close to the old-timers.

563
00:26:54,599 --> 00:26:55,920
Didn't you notice anything off?

564
00:27:05,119 --> 00:27:06,480
Close? Hardly.

565
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,319
Nobody has time for anyone else.

566
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:10,880
Everyone's busy with their own lives.

567
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,480
I went to see Cao Jun last night

568
00:27:20,359 --> 00:27:21,519
just to have a chat with him

569
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:24,240
about Old Qian.

570
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,359
If you could perform here one day,

571
00:27:42,839 --> 00:27:43,960
how awesome would that be?

572
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,359
You'd be a real pop star.

573
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:46,960
Go up there and blow them away!

574
00:27:47,319 --> 00:27:47,920
Yan!

575
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,799
Long time no see! Long time no see!

576
00:27:49,799 --> 00:27:50,599
Thanks! Thank you!

577
00:27:51,119 --> 00:27:52,400
Mr. Qian, Mr. Qian.

578
00:27:52,519 --> 00:27:53,079
Come on over.

579
00:27:53,319 --> 00:27:53,759
Mr. Qian.

580
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:54,720
Let me introduce him.

581
00:27:54,759 --> 00:27:55,960
This is Qian, Qian Yichuan.

582
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:56,319
That's right.

583
00:27:56,319 --> 00:27:56,880
Hello, hello.

584
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:57,640
Yu, hello, hello!

585
00:27:57,839 --> 00:27:58,559
Nice to meet you.

586
00:27:58,640 --> 00:27:58,960
Hello.

587
00:27:59,160 --> 00:28:00,519
Look at you, Yan, still so gorgeous!

588
00:28:02,279 --> 00:28:02,920
Oh, stop it.

589
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,880
I'm getting old.

590
00:28:05,359 --> 00:28:06,480
Qian here is super talented.

591
00:28:06,759 --> 00:28:08,079
So... what kind of artist are you?

592
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:10,279
I'm... I'm an accountant at our factory.

593
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:11,440
What?

594
00:28:12,079 --> 00:28:13,160
With a bachelor's degree.

595
00:28:13,799 --> 00:28:15,160
I like to sing a bit in my spare time.

596
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,160
Chunyan told me

597
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:18,680
that you're hiring singers here.

598
00:28:20,039 --> 00:28:22,359
Your stage looks really awesome.

599
00:28:22,759 --> 00:28:24,000
Of course. It's the best in town.

600
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:24,440
Right.

601
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,160
I was hoping to use your stage

602
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,359
to put my remaining energy to use,

603
00:28:27,599 --> 00:28:28,559
and show what I've got.

604
00:28:29,519 --> 00:28:30,680
Buddy, are you fifty?

605
00:28:30,839 --> 00:28:31,640
Me? No, not yet.

606
00:28:33,079 --> 00:28:33,920
I'm 47.

607
00:28:34,079 --> 00:28:34,680
Born in the year of the Rooster.

608
00:28:34,799 --> 00:28:35,559
Yu,

609
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,640
Qian sings with so much passion.

610
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:38,440
He's really good!

611
00:28:38,839 --> 00:28:39,720
Your voice is decent?

612
00:28:40,039 --> 00:28:40,640
Not bad.

613
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:43,039
I wanted to enter the Central Conservatory.

614
00:28:43,039 --> 00:28:43,839
My family thought it was too far,

615
00:28:43,839 --> 00:28:44,519
so they didn't let me go.

616
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:45,960
When I sing,

617
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,279
I usually project from the diaphragm.

618
00:28:48,039 --> 00:28:49,319
Look at the kids nowadays.

619
00:28:49,359 --> 00:28:51,440
They don't know where the diaphragm is.

620
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:53,519
You tighten your lower abdomen,

621
00:28:53,559 --> 00:28:54,440
push the breath up,

622
00:28:54,799 --> 00:28:55,519
and project your voice out.

623
00:28:55,839 --> 00:28:57,039
Once I stand up on that stage,

624
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:58,160
even without a mic,

625
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,000
sitting right where you are,

626
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,440
it'll sound crystal clear!

627
00:29:00,079 --> 00:29:01,200
Yu, let me tell you,

628
00:29:01,559 --> 00:29:02,799
Qian is truly talented.

629
00:29:03,039 --> 00:29:04,680
The anthem of our old Lapi Brewery?

630
00:29:04,799 --> 00:29:05,559
He wrote it.

631
00:29:05,599 --> 00:29:06,240
I wrote the lyrics.

632
00:29:07,559 --> 00:29:08,680
Then go ahead...

633
00:29:08,759 --> 00:29:09,880
sing a few lines for us.

634
00:29:10,599 --> 00:29:11,160
Give us a taste.

635
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:12,160
Wh-What should I sing?

636
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,519
Sing the factory anthem!

637
00:29:15,039 --> 00:29:15,440
Is that alright?

638
00:29:15,599 --> 00:29:15,839
Go for it.

639
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:16,319
Come on, let's hear it!

640
00:29:16,319 --> 00:29:16,720
Give him a hand!

641
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:17,240
Come on, come on.

642
00:29:18,799 --> 00:29:19,559
Put your glasses on.

643
00:29:19,599 --> 00:29:20,200
Come on, over here.

644
00:29:20,559 --> 00:29:21,079
Step right up.

645
00:29:22,119 --> 00:29:22,799
Make way, everyone.

646
00:29:24,519 --> 00:29:24,839
Yu.

647
00:29:24,839 --> 00:29:25,519
Come on, Yan, what are you doing...

648
00:29:25,599 --> 00:29:26,440
Put it behind, behind, behind.

649
00:29:26,559 --> 00:29:26,880
Okay.

650
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:27,319
Between you and me,

651
00:29:27,319 --> 00:29:28,559
why are you doing this?

652
00:29:28,559 --> 00:29:29,200
Just a small token.

653
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:30,000
Come on, take it, take it.

654
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:30,279
You really shouldn't have...

655
00:29:30,559 --> 00:29:32,359
Could you play the backing track for me?

656
00:29:32,519 --> 00:29:33,519
How professional!

657
00:29:33,839 --> 00:29:35,000
I'll find it. The sound system is great.

658
00:29:35,119 --> 00:29:35,759
It sure is.

659
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:36,920
I've been dying to try it out.

660
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:41,880
You've got this, Qian!

661
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:48,400
Three, two, one

662
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:48,880
Sing!

663
00:29:49,119 --> 00:29:52,759
Old Lacheng Brewery

664
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:56,480
Full of hope and sunshine

665
00:29:56,759 --> 00:29:59,920
The aroma of our beer

666
00:30:00,119 --> 00:30:03,759
Drifts far and wide

667
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:10,279
Old Lacheng Brewery

668
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:11,400
Brewery

669
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:14,119
Radiant and glorious, shining bright

670
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:15,279
Shining bright!

671
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:45,240
Good!

672
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:49,160
Nice!

673
00:30:56,359 --> 00:30:56,880
Wait...

674
00:30:56,880 --> 00:30:58,319
What's with this guy's leg?

675
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,359
What happened to his leg?

676
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:01,759
Well, he...

677
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:05,680
Buddy,

678
00:31:05,720 --> 00:31:07,039
what happened to your leg?

679
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:14,759
Well, see...

680
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:15,720
Back when...

681
00:31:16,680 --> 00:31:17,640
I did martial arts when I was young,

682
00:31:19,599 --> 00:31:20,480
loved doing flips,

683
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:21,720
and busted it up.

684
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:23,559
Doesn't slow me down, though.

685
00:31:23,960 --> 00:31:24,640
Not in the slightest.

686
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:25,480
I'm telling you,

687
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:26,359
if I pay attention,

688
00:31:26,359 --> 00:31:27,160
you can't even tell.

689
00:31:27,799 --> 00:31:28,680
I'm super agile.

690
00:31:36,599 --> 00:31:37,519
No issue at all.

691
00:31:37,599 --> 00:31:38,200
Are you all right?

692
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:38,599
I'm fine.

693
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:40,839
Let me take this call.

694
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:42,000
What's with you?

695
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,759
Have another one!

696
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:43,799
What are you doing?

697
00:31:58,920 --> 00:32:01,039
The factory anthem sounded amazing today!

698
00:32:01,559 --> 00:32:02,599
Haven't heard it in ages.

699
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:04,880
I got so moved, I almost cried.

700
00:32:05,119 --> 00:32:06,000
What was so good about it?

701
00:32:06,519 --> 00:32:07,160
I even forgot the lyrics.

702
00:32:07,880 --> 00:32:08,960
You sang it so well!

703
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:10,200
Look at that high note at the end!

704
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:13,119
Your breath was so steady.

705
00:32:13,119 --> 00:32:14,000
Really packed a punch!

706
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:15,400
High note? Come on.

707
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,400
My voice even cracked.

708
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:20,839
It's fine!

709
00:32:20,839 --> 00:32:21,759
What's the big deal?

710
00:32:22,039 --> 00:32:23,400
We got the gifts back anyway.

711
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:24,960
I've got plenty of buddies.

712
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:26,599
I reached out to other folks too.

713
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,079
I'll meet up with them in a few days.

714
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:28,880
We'll give it another shot.

715
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:29,240
Not going.

716
00:32:29,519 --> 00:32:30,000
It's humiliating.

717
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,400
Why not go?

718
00:32:32,400 --> 00:32:33,799
I chatted with them for a long time.

719
00:32:34,279 --> 00:32:35,160
How long did you chat?

720
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:36,839
All night long?

721
00:32:37,759 --> 00:32:38,599
How much money did you make?

722
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:44,759
Did you do the full package?

723
00:32:45,119 --> 00:32:45,960
Didn't take a dime.

724
00:32:46,039 --> 00:32:46,640
It was on the house.

725
00:32:47,359 --> 00:32:47,960
How about that?

726
00:32:48,039 --> 00:32:49,039
Ain't I good to you?

727
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:50,880
Fine.

728
00:32:54,559 --> 00:32:55,440
Listen...

729
00:32:56,559 --> 00:32:58,519
From now on, for a cripple like me,

730
00:32:59,279 --> 00:33:00,680
don't do those promotional stunts.

731
00:33:03,119 --> 00:33:04,079
I'm a lost cause anyway.

732
00:33:04,680 --> 00:33:06,880
In a few days, I'll find a watchman gig.

733
00:33:08,519 --> 00:33:09,119
Won't struggle anymore.

734
00:33:11,319 --> 00:33:12,119
Qian Yichuan!

735
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:17,160
I look down on you.

736
00:33:18,359 --> 00:33:19,680
Then stay forever in that abandoned plant,

737
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:20,759
guarding that crappy gate!

738
00:33:20,759 --> 00:33:21,799
I want to guard the gate!

739
00:33:22,599 --> 00:33:23,799
I love guarding the gate!

740
00:33:24,279 --> 00:33:25,680
I was born to guard gates!

741
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:26,599
What of it?

742
00:33:36,319 --> 00:33:36,839
Fine.

743
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,000
You're yelling at me now, huh?

744
00:33:40,319 --> 00:33:42,480
I don't feel sorry for you one bit now.

745
00:33:47,039 --> 00:33:48,759
I was so stupid when I was young.

746
00:33:50,039 --> 00:33:51,000
The first time I saw you,

747
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,400
I thought you had real backbone,

748
00:33:53,039 --> 00:33:54,359
that you'd make something of yourself.

749
00:33:55,279 --> 00:33:56,799
How did you become such a pathetic loser?

750
00:33:58,680 --> 00:33:59,359
If this place didn't work out,

751
00:33:59,359 --> 00:34:00,799
can't you just try somewhere else?

752
00:34:02,279 --> 00:34:03,519
What are you putting on an act for?

753
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,359
If you don't wanna live properly,

754
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,199
go ahead and die already!

755
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,599
Go die in place of good people!

756
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,480
Total waste buying you these clothes!

757
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:17,480
Waste of my money!

758
00:34:25,639 --> 00:34:26,159
Tu Chunyan!

759
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:27,519
Tu Chunyan!

760
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:28,599
What?!

761
00:35:08,559 --> 00:35:09,719
I haven't even taken off the tag.

762
00:35:12,639 --> 00:35:13,239
Take it back.

763
00:35:15,119 --> 00:35:15,880
Get lost.

764
00:35:24,559 --> 00:35:25,400
Get the hell out.

765
00:35:27,079 --> 00:35:27,920
Scram.

766
00:36:11,840 --> 00:36:13,159
Do you know that feeling?

767
00:36:14,519 --> 00:36:16,239
Like when I swallowed that list back then.

768
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:18,519
Couldn't swallow it down,

769
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,000
couldn't spit it out,

770
00:36:20,280 --> 00:36:20,920
just choking on it.

771
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,639
I'm just an idiot.

772
00:36:28,519 --> 00:36:29,960
Actually, Cao Jun is a good guy.

773
00:36:32,079 --> 00:36:32,960
In all these years,

774
00:36:34,039 --> 00:36:35,639
it was my first time going to his place.

775
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:39,199
If Old Qian hadn't pissed me off so badly,

776
00:36:40,599 --> 00:36:42,000
I wouldn't have gone over to chat.

777
00:36:44,320 --> 00:36:45,400
If I hadn't gone to his place,

778
00:36:47,199 --> 00:36:48,639
I wouldn't have become a suspect.

779
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:09,000
Life is just so hard.

780
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:11,119
Why does it have to be so exhausting?

781
00:37:14,719 --> 00:37:15,920
So many people got laid off.

782
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:18,320
Some people,

783
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,679
do whatever they can,

784
00:37:21,079 --> 00:37:22,480
just trying to survive.

785
00:37:25,599 --> 00:37:27,280
But why is Qian Yichuan like that?

786
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,840
Wasting his days just waiting to die,

787
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:32,800
always dwelling on the past,

788
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:33,639
unable to move on.

789
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:36,599
No matter what, I can't pull him out.

790
00:37:39,039 --> 00:37:40,519
Compared to how he used to be,

791
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:42,800
Old Qian has changed so much.

792
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:34,360
Look what time it is.

793
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:36,199
You're still in the mood for needlework?

794
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:39,079
Where are they?

795
00:38:40,559 --> 00:38:41,320
Go inside and take a seat first.

796
00:38:56,559 --> 00:38:57,239
Yan'er!

797
00:39:02,519 --> 00:39:03,000
You're here.

798
00:39:04,039 --> 00:39:05,239
Come on, have a seat inside.

799
00:39:05,599 --> 00:39:05,960
Okay.

800
00:39:28,519 --> 00:39:28,960
Chunyan.

801
00:39:29,440 --> 00:39:30,480
Go back, go sit over there.

802
00:39:30,880 --> 00:39:31,920
I like sitting next to you.

803
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:32,480
Got a problem?

804
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:39,880
Oh, boy.

805
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:41,639
Sorry I'm late!

806
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:42,800
Haipeng!

807
00:39:43,559 --> 00:39:44,280
Just waiting on me?

808
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:45,199
There's someone else.

809
00:39:46,760 --> 00:39:47,320
Who?

810
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:49,000
Isn't Tieping outside?

811
00:39:52,280 --> 00:39:53,039
Why are you sitting here?

812
00:39:53,760 --> 00:39:54,840
None of your business where I sit.

813
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:55,840
Just sit down already.

814
00:39:57,639 --> 00:39:58,320
Drink up.

815
00:40:01,599 --> 00:40:02,400
Hello, Master Liu.

816
00:40:02,599 --> 00:40:03,440
Hello, hello.

817
00:40:15,199 --> 00:40:16,239
Master, everyone is here.

818
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:18,400
Hello, everyone. Hello.

819
00:40:18,599 --> 00:40:19,320
Chief Engineer Chen.

820
00:40:19,360 --> 00:40:20,119
Chief Engineer Chen! Haipeng!

821
00:40:20,639 --> 00:40:21,440
What brings you here?

822
00:40:22,199 --> 00:40:22,840
Chief Engineer Chen.

823
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:24,280
Take the seat of honor.

824
00:40:26,119 --> 00:40:27,079
It's Chief Engineer Chen's dinner.

825
00:40:28,559 --> 00:40:29,000
Please sit.

826
00:40:33,119 --> 00:40:33,719
Where are you sitting?

827
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:34,440
Right here.

828
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:36,159
Thank you. Thank you.

829
00:40:36,519 --> 00:40:38,639
It's been years since I retired.

830
00:40:39,079 --> 00:40:39,760
And I haven't...

831
00:40:40,079 --> 00:40:41,039
really gotten out

832
00:40:42,519 --> 00:40:43,119
to socialize much.

833
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,400
Well...

834
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:46,719
with two murder cases

835
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,440
happening lately,

836
00:40:49,679 --> 00:40:51,079
I figured if not for this,

837
00:40:51,639 --> 00:40:52,519
us old buddies

838
00:40:52,719 --> 00:40:54,199
would rarely get together.

839
00:40:55,519 --> 00:40:55,920
Come on.

840
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:57,599
Let me propose a toast.

841
00:40:57,679 --> 00:40:58,199
Cheers!

842
00:40:58,239 --> 00:40:59,079
Chief Engineer Chen always treats us.

843
00:40:59,079 --> 00:41:00,039
You're a rare guest.

844
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:01,519
We actually meet up all the time.

845
00:41:02,039 --> 00:41:02,440
That's right.

846
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:04,800
Haipeng foots the bill every time.

847
00:41:05,039 --> 00:41:05,679
Super generous.

848
00:41:06,079 --> 00:41:06,880
Least I could do.

849
00:41:07,440 --> 00:41:08,239
Haipeng's doing well.

850
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:09,519
With that wedding business,

851
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:10,639
he makes good money.

852
00:41:11,119 --> 00:41:12,239
Always showing off, though.

853
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:13,960
Quit your blabbering.

854
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:15,199
All right, all right.

855
00:41:17,440 --> 00:41:18,119
Chief Engineer Chen,

856
00:41:18,639 --> 00:41:19,239
you propose one.

857
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:20,159
Right, you propose a toast.

858
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:23,159
Come on.

859
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:24,280
To Cao Jun.

860
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:24,719
Well...

861
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:31,280
Right.

862
00:41:41,119 --> 00:41:41,639
Hey,

863
00:41:45,079 --> 00:41:46,840
look what they're saying on TV.

864
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:49,599
In Cao Jun and Ma Guowen's...

865
00:41:49,679 --> 00:41:50,679
in this case,

866
00:41:51,079 --> 00:41:53,199
both of them died the exact same way.

867
00:41:54,039 --> 00:41:55,800
Plastic bags over their heads,

868
00:41:56,119 --> 00:41:58,480
and beer bottle caps on their bodies.

869
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:00,639
The way I see it,

870
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:02,880
it was definitely the same person.

871
00:42:03,679 --> 00:42:05,400
It's a serial murder case.

872
00:42:06,480 --> 00:42:07,440
We just don't know

873
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:09,519
who the next one is.

874
00:42:11,639 --> 00:42:12,239
Yeah.

875
00:42:13,360 --> 00:42:15,079
They both had beer bottle caps.

876
00:42:16,039 --> 00:42:16,760
Back then,

877
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,880
when Liu Xuemei died,

878
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:21,480
there was a beer bottle cap next to her.

879
00:42:23,039 --> 00:42:24,239
When Xuemei died,

880
00:42:24,239 --> 00:42:25,440
why was there a beer bottle cap?

881
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,320
How should I know?

882
00:42:28,639 --> 00:42:30,440
I just saw a glimpse of it on the news,

883
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:31,320
and it stuck with me.

884
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:33,199
Ma Guowen got what he deserved.

885
00:42:34,679 --> 00:42:35,519
Liu Xuemei...

886
00:42:36,039 --> 00:42:36,880
she had it coming too.

887
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:38,480
What are you saying?

888
00:42:38,679 --> 00:42:39,239
What?

889
00:42:39,519 --> 00:42:40,639
If not for her,

890
00:42:41,199 --> 00:42:42,840
would we have ended up like this?

891
00:42:44,239 --> 00:42:45,840
You ruined your own life, who's to blame?

892
00:42:46,199 --> 00:42:46,880
Blame who?

893
00:42:48,079 --> 00:42:48,519
Right.

894
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:49,639
I can't blame anyone.

895
00:42:49,679 --> 00:42:50,559
What about Cao Jun?

896
00:42:52,039 --> 00:42:53,360
What about Cao Jun?

897
00:42:53,519 --> 00:42:54,880
Who did he ever cross?

898
00:42:55,559 --> 00:42:56,800
Cautious his entire life,

899
00:42:56,800 --> 00:42:58,000
scared of his own shadow.

900
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:00,440
He drove a forklift just fine,

901
00:43:00,519 --> 00:43:01,519
then sold tea eggs,

902
00:43:01,679 --> 00:43:03,440
and then drove a tuk-tuk.

903
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:05,679
Now someone's gone and killed him.

904
00:43:06,440 --> 00:43:07,320
And for what?

905
00:43:08,559 --> 00:43:09,840
Isn't it all because of that whore?

906
00:43:10,239 --> 00:43:11,159
That's enough!

907
00:43:11,719 --> 00:43:12,400
Qian Yichuan!

908
00:43:12,559 --> 00:43:13,280
She's already dead.

909
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:14,320
Have some decency!

910
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:15,400
Can't talk about the dead?

911
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,519
Drink up, let's talk about the living.

912
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:17,760
What do you mean?

913
00:43:18,239 --> 00:43:19,840
What's the deal with your ex-wife?

914
00:43:20,079 --> 00:43:21,119
Why did she come back?

915
00:43:21,119 --> 00:43:22,559
To make a film for Ma Guowen?

916
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:23,960
Is she on your side,

917
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:25,239
or is she with Ma Guowen?

918
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,079
Back then... You just never quit, do you?

919
00:43:26,079 --> 00:43:27,519
Was she one of the people who betrayed us?

920
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:33,199
Don't move.

921
00:43:33,239 --> 00:43:33,480
Me?

922
00:43:33,480 --> 00:43:34,000
Qian Yichuan.

923
00:43:34,559 --> 00:43:35,119
Let go!

924
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:36,199
If you've got the balls,

925
00:43:36,360 --> 00:43:37,199
hit me right here.

926
00:43:37,599 --> 00:43:38,360
If beating me to death

927
00:43:38,360 --> 00:43:39,159
satisfies you,

928
00:43:39,320 --> 00:43:39,920
then go ahead and hit me!

929
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:47,599
Where are you going?

930
00:43:48,079 --> 00:43:49,039
I'm talking to you!

931
00:43:49,920 --> 00:43:50,639
Don't move!

932
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:53,199
I just want to know how she really died.

933
00:43:53,239 --> 00:43:54,760
What happened to her before she died?

934
00:43:55,400 --> 00:43:56,199
She froze to death.

935
00:43:57,480 --> 00:43:59,079
Why can't you just let this go?
